all right let me talk about something  that that happened over the weekend  um as many of you know uh when the  latest  israeli-palestinian uh flare-up  took place um at first  for the first four or so days i i didn't  say anything about it  feeling i didn't really have too much to  add i heard from some people  respectfully who said hey you should  talk about this  um and then so i did and i did a  20-minute segment it's over the last  month it's the only 20-minute segment  i've done and that was a couple of weeks  ago and throughout  before i talked about it and after the  anti-semitic comments raining down on  our youtube channel  raining down on twitter instagram we  we've had to block  tw twitch thousands uh close to a  thousand people i would say i don't want  to exaggerate  certainly hundreds of people on youtube  about a hundred on uh on twitter  call it 600 to 800 people probably okay  to not not be hyperbolic which is you  know a lot for a program our size  and even after i did the segment the  anti-semitic comments about me being a  jew rat or all of this different stuff  they just didn't stop and at a certain  point it sort of becomes clear that  you're not really  contacting me about foreign policy  anymore it's just anti-semitism that's  really what it is  this crossed over to the real world and  over the weekend i was  um out with some friends for dinner uh  at um at a restaurant and  um we were there sort of a lot of things  are still closing early in the northeast  um because of covid guidelines and so  there were very few people left  and as i was leaving um i walked by  someone  who kind of gave me a weird look and i  didn't know if it was  that you know i had some borscht on my  face like that one time where i did an  entire show  with with borscht on my face and  producer pat didn't tell me  or maybe they recognized me i didn't  really know walked past them  and when i'm 30 feet away um  i hear pacman and i turn around  and they yell at me you jew  zionist imperialist  now uh i just turned and walked away i  didn't  engage with it and i think in general  what these people want  is a reaction and who knows if they plan  to film me and put it on twitter or  whatever the case  um but i just i just walked away  and you know this what what's really  obviously this is not fun um but  people come up to me all the time and  typically they're  they're positive experiences and i do a  show that's public and so  to some degree this is this is bound to  happen but  um you know this is this was a quote  left winger  right this this is not a right winger  this is an issue that it's it's more  often the left  the right does a lot of anti-semitism  with me uh but they say go back to  israel  right the right-wing anti-semitism is go  back to israel a place i've been once in  my life for  nine days um the this is this was some  something from the left  and so i think it should be clear to all  of us at this point  that this is not a critique of my  position  right it's not it's not even really an  argument as many of you know  uh i have more than a decade on record  of being  unquestionably critical of uh  settlements  the netanyahu administration the urgency  with which we need to find a way to lift  the blockade  i'm not going to do the segment and see  this is the problem  why am i even talking about policy  because this incident was not about  policy  i've spoken about you know the  israeli-palestinian conflict  really once in the last two years and so  jew zionist imperialist um is not even  plausibly  a critique of my policy and uh  all sorts of things are going off here  so what do we do about something like  this  i don't know i don't really plan to do  anything about it  there's a there's a real problem with  anti-semitism on the right and we've  covered it for a really long time we  just reviewed on a recent live stream  uh that white nationalist dude who  wanted craig cobb who wanted a  whites-only enclave  in one of the dakotas and he was overtly  anti-semitic during our interview and  that's very clearly a right-wing  anti-semitism  unfortunately there's a left-wing  anti-semitism as well  and uh even by talking about this  there's going to be even more that's  hurled at me and some people are going  to write and say  well it's not anti-semitism david  because you are a zionist and as i've  always said before  what do you even mean by that term every  time i've been confronted with it  um i never really get a straight answer  and what i've said before is if what  you're asking me is do i  think that the solution to the  israeli-palestinian conflict is no more  israel  no i don't think that's the solution  much like  the solution is not no no palestinian  state  right i think the solution is an israeli  state in a palestinian state  does it does that make me a zionist uh  because otherwise it's never anything  we're able to actually figure out but  hurling jew  zionist imperialist to someone you know  on the street  um is is over the line it's not a policy  critique  i don't know what else to say about it  but if the left goes  too far in this direction um  it's not going to be good and as i said  before  it's counterproductive it's  counterproductive because  every time jewish folks hear  about not what happened to me what  happened to me was not violent wasn't  physically violent but what we  we've the videos we saw from los angeles  new york etc  more and more american jews or jews  wherever they're being harassed in  france  say wow i really may need  to move to israel someday and they  disengage  from holding israel accountable for the  things israel does wrong so not only do  i think it's ugly and disgusting  it's also counterproductive to what most  of these leftists claim to want  i think that's all i really feel the  need to say about it  maybe something i'll follow up on at  some point in the future but  really ugly stuff unbecoming unbecoming  of the left

